            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0181" n="171" xml:id="pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.34 Leasing/124</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-24">August 24, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        31.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to recent reports concerning the
                    possible lease of six United States destroyers to Brazil, I have the honor to
                    report that the Minister for Foreign Affairs showed me yesterday a telegram from
                    Dr. Rodriguez Alvarez, Brazilian representative on the Chaco Commission, which
                    set out that the recent declaration issued jointly by the United States and
                    Brazilian Governments had had an excellent effect at Buenos Aires. Dr. Rodriguez
                    Alvarez added, however, that in his opinion further publicity in this matter
                    should be avoided at this juncture. Dr. Pimentel Brandão remarked to me that the
                    Brazilian Government concurred in that opinion.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
